DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       GGAASSHH is Bash, but in BroStyle.

       That's all, bro!

       FFuunn ffaacctt:: I'm planning to bring 2026 slang into this project.  The ter-
       minal is about to get a vocabulary upgrade. =D

OOPPTTIIOONNSS
       GASH is based on GNU Bash, so its command syntax and options are gener-
       ally  inherited  from  Bash. Some output and error-message behavior may
       differ because of GASH customizations.

       Here are some common options:

       --cc _c_o_m_m_a_n_d___s_t_r_i_n_g
              Execute commands from _c_o_m_m_a_n_d___s_t_r_i_n_g, then exit.

              BBrrooTTiipp:: Wrap a command string in quotes when it contains  spaces
              or shell metacharacters, for example: ggaasshh --cc ''ggiitt rreemmoottee --vv''

       --nn _f_i_l_e
              Read commands and check their syntax without executing them.

              WWaarrnniinngg::  This  checks  shell  syntax, not whether your script's
              logic is correct or whether it will behave as you expect.

              BBrrooTTiipp:: Want to catch  more  potential  script  problems?   Give
              sshheellllcchheecckk(1) a try. It's free. =D

       --ll, ----llooggiinn
              Make GASH act as if it had been invoked as a login shell.

       For  the  complete  list  of options, see bbaasshh(1) or the Bash reference
       documentation.

